  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 1243 AM MDT Tue Sep 29 2026\n\nSome lingering showers/storms across northeast NM Thursday on the \nbackside of the exiting upper low along with gusty north winds \nbehind a potent backdoor front. Some wind advisories may need to be \nissued for the northeast highlands and plains. Temperatures rebound \ncloser to average across western and central NM Thursday Streams and \nrivers will be higher and fast flowing during this time as the early \nweek rainfall moves downstream through various channels. The \nbackdoor front pushes through the rest of eastern NM Thursday \nafternoon resulting in breezy north winds. The upper high over the \neastern Pacific Thursday moves east to over the Great Basin and Four \nCorners Friday and this weekend resulting in a splendid 1st weekend \nof October. High temperatures outside of mountain peaks will be in \nthe mid 60s to mid 70s. Fog will be a concern, especially in valley \nlocations, during the early to mid morning hours each day during \nthis time due to the saturated grounds in place.",
